# ⚠️  .hf_cache MUST STAY EXCLUDED — TWO SEPARATE REASONS.
#
# 1. IT BREAKS THE BUILD. HuggingFace stores each file once under blobs/ and
#    symlinks it into snapshots/. Docker's build-context loader cannot follow
#    those links and fails outright:
#
#      failed to solve: invalid file request .hf_cache/hub/
#      models--cross-encoder--ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2/snapshots/.../
#      special_tokens_map.json
#
# 2. IT DOES NOT BELONG IN THE IMAGE ANYWAY. The cache is bind-mounted at
#    runtime (./backend/.hf_cache:/root/.cache/huggingface) precisely so the
#    models survive `docker-compose down -v`. Baking a 183MB copy into the
#    build context re-transfers it on every build and pins stale weights into
#    the image.
.hf_cache/

# Python
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Secrets — live API keys. Never in an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Virtualenvs
.venv
venv

# Runtime data. These are volumes at run time; a copy in the image would
# shadow the mount on first start and confuse debugging.
uploads/
images/

# Evaluation output — regenerated by eval/run_eval.py, not part of the app.
eval/results/

# Local tooling
.git
.gitignore
*.md
